[02:30.06] Ticking away the moments that make up a dull day
[02:37.07] You fritter and waste the hours in an offhand way
[02:44.47] Kicking around on a piece of ground in your hometown
[02:51.93] Waiting for someone or something to show you the way
[02:59.50] Tired of lying in the sunshine
[03:03.13] Staying home to watch the rain
[03:07.30] And you are young and life is long
[03:10.42] And there is time to kill today
[03:15.43] And then one day you find
[03:18.74] Ten years have got behind you
[03:22.54] No one told you when to run
[03:26.51] You missed the starting gun
[03:29.86] And you run, and you run to catch up with the sun
[03:35.03] 
[04:59.69] But it's sinking
[05:03.16] Racing around to come up behind you again
[05:10.70] The sun is the same in a relative way
[05:13.87] But you're older
[05:17.55] Shorter of breath, and one day closer to death
[05:24.78] Every year is getting shorter
[05:28.24] Never seem to find the time
[05:31.62] Plans that either come to naught
[05:35.72] Or half a page of scribbled lines
[05:39.98] Hanging on in quiet desperation
[05:43.17] Is the English way
[05:47.74] The time is gone, the song is over
[05:50.96] Thought I'd something more to say
[05:55.39] 
[06:12.25] Home, home again
[06:17.06] 
[06:19.74] I like to be here when I can
[06:25.27] 
[06:27.70] When I come home cold and tired
[06:32.92] 
[06:34.96] It's good to warm my bones beside the fire
